<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.9.4: Expressions in Standard Form</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01881</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.9.4: Expressions in Standard Form</md:title>
    <md:uuid>150adc77-4c4a-46bf-8099-f20858903cae</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down 5 min</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>For each expression, write an equivalent expression in standard form. Show your reasoning.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((2x+5)(x+1)\)</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(2x^2+7x+5\). The diagram shows that\((2x+5)(x+1)=2x \cdot x+2x \cdot 1+5 \cdot x+5 \cdot
  1\). Adding this together gives \(2x^2+7x+5\) in standard form.</para>
<table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis"/>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(2x\)</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(5\)</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
      <entry>\(2x^2\)</entry>
      <entry>\(5x\)</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(1\)</entry>
      <entry>\(2x\)</entry>
      <entry>\(5\)</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x-2)(x+2)\)</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x^2-4\). \((x+2)(x-2)=x^2+(-2x)+2x+(-4)=x^2-4\). The diagram also shows that
  \((x+2)(x-2)=x^2-4\).</para>
<table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis"/>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(2\)</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
      <entry>\(x^2\)</entry>
      <entry>\(2x\)</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(-2\)</entry>
      <entry>\(-2x\)</entry>
      <entry>\(-4\)</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table></section>
</content>
</document>
